config BR2_PACKAGE_AR8030_TRANSPORT_RX
	bool "ar8030-transport-rx"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_AR8030
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
	help
	  Ground-side bridge from the AR8030's non-IP baseband data
	  channel (bb_socket) to PixelPilot_rk -- see
	  https://github.com/henkwiedig/ar8030-transport.

	  Reassembles the chunks ar8030-transport-tx sends from the air
	  unit's waybeam frame-shm ring, RTP/H.265-packetizes each
	  completed frame, and forwards it over UDP to PixelPilot's own
	  RTP listener (its "-p" flag, default 5600). No PixelPilot_rk
	  source changes -- a stock pixelpilot binary is the intended
	  consumer.

	  Requires this project's own ar8030 package patch
	  0008-session_socket-preserve-datagram-flag-on-open.patch (see
	  ar8030-transport's README "Required AR8030 SDK fix" -- without
	  it on *both* ends of the link, chunks above ~690 bytes fail).

	  Also builds, installs, and starts ar8030-lifecycled (see
	  ar8030-transport's README "ar8030-lifecycled: link supervisor +
	  bind button") and its ifup/ifdown and connect/drop beep
	  (playsong.sh, board/caddx/vrxpro's own overlay) hooks -- moved
	  here from S97ar8030 (package/ar8030) now that this package is
	  what actually builds the binary; see S98ar8030-transport-rx's own
	  comment for the reset-backend/role difference from the air side.

	  Installs /usr/bin/ar8030-transport-rx, /usr/bin/ar8030-linkctl,
	  /usr/bin/ar8030-lifecycled, and /etc/init.d/S98ar8030-transport-rx.

	  Also installs /usr/bin/ascent-ota, which updates a Caddx Ascent
	  air unit over the link: it serves an ASW image over HTTP on
	  ar_net0 (or copies it over ssh where python3 is missing) and runs
	  the air's sysupgrade --asw=<url|file> --copy-overlay.

	  And /usr/bin/p1-ota, the same for a BetaFPV P1 air unit: it copies
	  an OpenIPC P1_SKY_*.img into the air's /tmp over ssh and runs the
	  air's sysupgrade on it, which keeps the settings and pairing.
	  A stock image puts BetaFPV's or SinYine's stock firmware back.

	  /usr/bin/air-ota picks the one for an image by its header;
	  PixelPilot's Drone -> Actions -> OTA update runs it.

	  And /usr/bin/ar8030-xdata, which writes to the ground chip's host
	  data channel; the chips carry it to the air chip's UART2 (the
	  Caddx Ascent's gimbal pads). `ar8030-xdata relay` forwards UDP
	  datagrams from 127.0.0.1:5770 there, e.g. gs-headtrack's gimbal
	  frames (the VRX Pro's S99headtrack).

if BR2_PACKAGE_AR8030_TRANSPORT_RX

config BR2_PACKAGE_AR8030_TRANSPORT_RX_KMOD
	bool "SDIO kernel module (artosyn_drv)"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_AR8030_BUS_SDIO
	help
	  Builds ar8030-transport's clean-room kernel module (kmod/:
	  artosyn_drv.ko, the SDIO chardev /dev/artosyn_sdio that ar8030d
	  -i 1 talks to, plus the native ar_net0 net_device) for a board
	  whose AR8030 sits on SDIO. It pushes the baseband firmware and
	  config (fw_name=, cfg_name=) when the chip enumerates in boot-ROM
	  mode and stays loaded. Same module OpenIPC/builder's
	  ar8030-transport-tx builds for the air units.

endif

comment "ar8030-transport-rx needs ar8030 and a toolchain w/ threads"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_AR8030 || !BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
